CommitDate: Tue Nov 24 12:21:44 2026 +0000

    Fix economy disk forecast inflation from one-off reclaims
    
    forecast_hours used the oldest sample in the 2-24h lookback as one endpoint,
    so a single reclamation inside the window made net loss look tiny and produced
    a wildly inflated time-to-full (1296h where the sustained rate implies ~38h).
    Use the median of positive net-loss rates over the most recent six hours,
    excluding reclaim intervals, with whole-lookback and single-sample fallbacks.
    Add a smoke-test regression. Economy proceed request P-1795522620-c40b.

diff --git a/government/economy-resources.py b/government/economy-resources.py
